#!/usr/bin/env python3

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# cyview – Handoff Summary (for future maintenance)
#
# Purpose
# -------
# cyview is a small Linux CLI tool that displays Cytoscape.js JSON graphs
# ("CYJS", typically stored as *.cyjs). It is meant to be a generic viewer that
# other tools can invoke after generating CYJS output, and can be registered as
# the handler for the .cyjs extension so xdg-open/file managers open graphs.
#
# High-level behavior
# -------------------
# - Reads CYJS either from:
#     * a file path argument (graph.cyjs)
#     * stdin (explicit '-' or piped input)
# - Creates a temp session directory containing:
#     * viewer.html (Cytoscape.js page)
#     * the CYJS file (served via local HTTP)
# - Starts a tiny local HTTP server (ThreadingHTTPServer)
# - Opens the viewer via:
#     * Chromium/Chrome in --app mode (preferred, if available + GUI)
#     * otherwise xdg-open
#     * or --ui print-url which prints the URL and does not open a browser
# - In Chromium mode, cyview waits for Chromium to close and then exits.
#   In xdg-open mode, it cannot detect browser closure reliably; it runs until
#   Ctrl+C or until --once triggers (best-effort).
#
# CLI options (current design)
# ----------------------------
# - --ui {auto|chromium|xdg-open|print-url}
# - --bind ADDR (default 127.0.0.1)
# - --port PORT (default 0 = ephemeral)
# - --once      : exit after viewer.html is first served (best-effort)
# - --emit json : machine-readable output (url/bind/port/ui/source/styles)
# - --keep-alive: debugging; don't auto-exit on chromium close
#
# Styling system (key feature)
# ----------------------------
# cyview dynamically builds Cytoscape style selector blocks:
#
# 1) Start with hard-coded DEFAULT_STYLES in the script
#    (includes text wrapping, label backgrounds for readability, etc.)
#
# 2) Then apply zero or more external style files (JSON) in this order:
#      /etc/cyview/
#      ~/.config/cyview/
#      <cyjs file directory>   (only when input is a file)
#      <current working directory (PWD)>
#
# 3) Styles files are named by a "scheme":
#      scheme=default -> "cyview.styles"
#      scheme=NAME    -> "cyview.styles.NAME"
#
# 4) Scheme selection precedence:
#      --styles NAME (CLI) overrides
#      else CYVIEW_STYLES env var
#      else default
#
# 5) Styles file format:
#      - JSON array of selector blocks, OR
#      - JSON object containing {"style": [...]} or {"styles": [...]}
#
# 6) Replace semantics:
#      If the first line (leading whitespace allowed) is "# replace",
#      the running style list is cleared before appending JSON that follows.
#      If nothing follows "# replace", the resulting style list is empty.
#
# 7) Merge semantics:
#      Style blocks are appended; later blocks override earlier ones when
#      selectors overlap (Cytoscape.js resolves later styles last).
#
# 8) Tab-completion helper:
#      `--styles list` prints discovered scheme names (one per line) and exits.
#      Discovery scans the same search directories for cyview.styles and
#      cyview.styles.* files. Always includes "default".
#
# Important bug/lesson learned (HTML_TEMPLATE)
# -------------------------------------------
# We initially had a blank page with:
#   viewer.html: Uncaught SyntaxError: Unexpected token '{'
# Root causes:
# - Template contained double braces "{{" / "}}" (leftover from .format() style),
#   which broke JavaScript syntax when we switched to .replace().
# - Inlining JSON as a JS literal inside <script> can be fragile.
#
# Fix:
# - Use a clean HTML_TEMPLATE with normal braces.
# - Embed the styles JSON in a <script type="application/json"> tag and parse it
#   via JSON.parse(), rather than injecting as code.
# - Use json.dumps(..., ensure_ascii=True) when embedding JSON text.
#
# Debugging workflow
# ------------------
# - Use: `cyview --ui print-url --emit json graph.cyjs`
# - Open URL in a normal browser window and use DevTools Console/Network:
#   * syntax errors => template/JSON injection problem
#   * failed fetch  => serving/path issue
#   * cytoscape undefined => CDN load/network issue
#
# Man page
# --------
# Documentation is maintained as `cyview.1` (section 1 CLI tool), covering:
# - usage, input format, options
# - styles configuration, scheme naming, search order
# - CYVIEW_STYLES env var
# - --styles list for tab completion
#
# Bash completion (external snippet)
# ---------------------------------
# Bash completion was built to complete:
# - flags
# - --ui values
# - --emit values
# - --styles schemes using `cyview --styles list`
# - positional *.cyjs files (and directories) using filename completion options
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------


